%description:

Tcp.fastopenBlackholeTimeout:other -- 5 s after a black hole, the SYN has no Fast Open option; 15 s after it, a Fast Open option.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "TCP Fast Open, client: when a SYN with a Fast Open option or data times out
the second time, so that it goes the third time (a negative response, RFC 7413 section 4.1.3.1),
no connection uses Fast Open for this time ...; 0s: no detection".

The classes: hour (3600 s, the default), other (another value), off (0 s, the value of
LinuxTcp: no detection). The code: TcpConnection::process_TIMEOUT_SYN_REXMIT() records a black
hole when a SYN with a Fast Open option or data goes the third time;
Tcp::recordFastOpenBlackhole() then stops Fast Open for the value, and
TcpConnection::process_OPEN_ACTIVE() opens without it. This test separates "other" from the other values.

Host under test: host1, a Fast Open client; host2 is a Fast Open server (preconditions). host1
opens connection 1 at 0.1 s with Fast Open; the tap drops the SYNs of host1 in the first 2.5 s,
so the SYN goes at 0.1 s, 1.1 s and the third time at 3.1 s. host1 opens connection 2 at 8.1 s
and connection 3 at 18.1 s with Fast Open and 500 bytes, 5 s and 15 s after the black hole. A Fast
Open option is a cookie request or, after a cookie, the cookie. Observation: level 1, the SYN of connection 2 has no Fast Open option, and the SYN of connection 3 has a Fast Open option.

%# parameter: Tcp.fastopenBlackholeTimeout
%# class: other
%# value: 10s
%# key: *.host1.tcp.fastopenBlackholeTimeout
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpMutations.h"
#include "TcpTestApp.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpFastopenBlackholeTimeoutOther")
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host1").filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true").drop().within(2.5)
                     .describe("each SYN of host1 in the first 2.5 s"))
        .act(action().at(0.1).run<TcpTestApp>("host1.app[0]", [](TcpTestApp& app) { app.socket().connect(app.addressOf("host2"), 1000, true); })
                 .describe("host1 opens connection 1 with Fast Open"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .describe("the first SYN of connection 1")
             .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .describe("the second SYN of connection 1")
             .within(1.5))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .describe("the third SYN of connection 1: a black hole")
             .within(2.5))
        .act(action().at(8.1).run<TcpTestApp>("host1.app[1]", [](TcpTestApp& app) { app.socket().connect(app.addressOf("host2"), 1000, true); app.sendData(app.socket(), 500); })
                 .describe("host1 opens connection 2 with Fast Open, and sends 500 bytes"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
                  .first()
                  .assertEvent([](const MatchContext& context) {
                      std::string cookie = tcpFastOpenCookieOf(context.event.packet);
                      return cookie == "-";
                  })
                  .describe("the SYN of connection 2: no Fast Open option")
                  .within(0.5))
        .act(action().at(18.1).run<TcpTestApp>("host1.app[2]", [](TcpTestApp& app) { app.socket().connect(app.addressOf("host2"), 1000, true); app.sendData(app.socket(), 500); })
                 .describe("host1 opens connection 3 with Fast Open, and sends 500 bytes"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
                  .first()
                  .assertEvent([](const MatchContext& context) {
                      std::string cookie = tcpFastOpenCookieOf(context.event.packet);
                      return cookie != "-";
                  })
                  .describe("the SYN of connection 3: a Fast Open option")
                  .within(0.5));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpFastopenBlackholeTimeoutOther compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.fastopenBlackholeTimeout = 10s    # the parameter under test
*.host2.tcp.fastopenServerEnabled = true
*.host1.tcp.fastopenClientEnabled = true
*.host1.numApps = 3
*.host1.app[*].typename = "TcpTestApp"
sim-time-limit = 20s
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpFastopenBlackholeTimeoutOther: PASS
